WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.215
A jar of syrup can look trustworthy while concealing an

00:00:05.215 --> 00:00:08.551
unstable preparation. That difficulty was familiar to

00:00:08.551 --> 00:00:10.934
pharmacists long before industrial manufacturing.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.509
A prescription was not finished when its ingredients

00:00:19.509 --> 00:00:22.950
were combined. In medieval Cairo, a medicine still had

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.479
to be made reliable.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.917
The Minhaj al-dukkan associated with al-Kuhin al-Attar

00:00:34.917 --> 00:00:38.383
documents practical pharmaceutical choices. It is an

00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:41.850
historical text, not a modern clinical trial.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.768
Concentration, ingredients and preservation are

00:00:48.768 --> 00:00:52.941
questions of practice. A formula means little if the

00:00:52.941 --> 00:00:56.186
preparation changes before it reaches its user.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:05.507
A pharmacist with an unavailable ingredient had to

00:01:05.507 --> 00:01:08.550
consider replacement. Similar names or therapeutic

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:11.593
intentions did not guarantee material equivalence.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.027
A prescription from the Cairo Genizah is a different

00:01:20.027 --> 00:01:23.604
kind of source from a formulary. Its surviving words

00:01:23.604 --> 00:01:26.386
can reveal a particular documentary practice, without

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.373
describing every pharmacy in Cairo.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.956
The historical question is how makers judged

00:01:34.956 --> 00:01:37.461
concentration, consistency and suitable substitution.

00:01:37.461 --> 00:01:41.468
Those are decisions visible in instructions, even when

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:45.475
the preparation itself no longer survives for chemical

00:01:45.475 --> 00:01:45.976
testing.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.231
The historical evidence shows attempts to make medicine

00:01:51.231 --> 00:01:54.540
dependable. It does not justify calling medieval

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.431
practice modern quality assurance.
